(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-08-30"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-08-30","label":"2026 年 8 月 30 日","date":"2026-08-30","range":"","theme":"科技","themes":["科技"],"sources":["Economist"],"title":"Without a trace","titleZh":"污影消痕","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":9,"vocab":35,"question":15,"qa":0,"original":4,"layout":1},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"8.30 精读(1).pdf","headline":{"title":"Without a trace","titleZh":"污影消痕","source":"Economist","series":"考研那些事儿之科技系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"Good news on global warming is thin on the ground. But there may be some up in the air. Operation Blue Skies, announced on August 18th, is a scientific study being undertaken by Britain’s air-traffic-control service, NATS, and various organisations where people study the effects on climate of the streaks of cloud created by aircraft—known as contrails.","zh":"在广袤的大地上，关于全球变暖的好消息寥寥无几。但在高空之上或许还有一些转机。8月18日，英国空中交通管制服务机构NATS与多个气候研究机构共同开展的科学研究宣布启动，名为“蓝天行动”。研究人员专门研究飞机产生的条状云，即所谓的飞机尾迹云对气候的影响。"},{"index":2,"en":"Over the next two winters the consortium aims to see if it is possible to reduce the number of persistent contrails—the class with the largest such effects—over a swathe of the North Atlantic, thereby measurably reducing the climate impact of civil aviation. If this experiment works, a worldwide application of the same techniques might cut the climate effects of air travel by as much as half.","zh":"在接下来的两个冬天，研究团队计划考察，能否通过减少北大西洋大片空域中持久性尾迹云量，从而显著降低民航对气候的影响。这类尾迹云产生的气候影响最大。如果这项实验取得成功，再将这项技术应用到全球范围，或许可以将航空旅行对气候造成的影响降低半数之多。"},{"index":3,"en":"On a sunny day the wispy cirrus clouds into which some contrails are transformed can look as if they might be cooling the planet in the manner of a delicate parasol. And some contrails do indeed cool things down beneath them a bit. But they also warm things up by trapping some of the upwelling infrared radiation that would otherwise escape into space. On average, that warming effect, found in all contrails (and the cirrus clouds they turn into), handsomely outweighs the cooling provided by some. In the climate scheme of things, contrails are a liability.","zh":"在阳光明媚的日子里，一些飞机尾迹云会逐渐转化为纤细的卷云，看起来仿佛一把精巧的遮阳伞，似乎能够为地球降温。事实上，部分尾迹云确实会让其下方的气温略有下降。但与此同时，它们也会通过截留一部分原本会逸散到太空中的上升红外辐射，使地球升温。平均而言，这种增温效应存在于所有尾迹云（以及它们最终转化成的卷云）中，其作用远远超过了部分尾迹云所带来的降温效果。从气候大局来看，尾迹云是一项负担。"},{"index":4,"en":"Happily, it appears that much harm can be avoided by small changes to flight paths. Persistent contrails appear only in what are known as “ice- supersaturated regions” (ISSRs). Often planes can avoid such regions just by flying a little bit lower. The purpose of Operation Blue Skies is to find out how well the presence of ISSRs can be predicted, how effective such little shifts in altitude can be in avoiding persistent contrails, and how easily and safely the changes in flight path needed to bring them about can be integrated into routines for airlines and air-traffic control.","zh":"好在，似乎只需对飞行航线做些小幅调整，就能避免其中相当一部分危害。持久性尾迹云只会出现在所谓的“冰过饱和区”内。飞机往往只需稍微降低飞行高度，就可以避开这些区域。“蓝天行动”的目的，就是弄清楚以下几个问题：ISSR的存在能否被准确预测；如此小幅的高度调整在多大程度上能够有效避免持久性尾迹云；以及，为实现这一目的所需的航线调整，如何能以便捷且安全的方式纳入航空公司和空中交通管制的日常运行流程。"},{"index":5,"en":"The cut of up to half in the climate-effects of air travel would come at a very small cost. The number of flights at lowered altitude might be small—as little as 5% of the total. Because altitude buys efficiency, those flights would consume more jet fuel, but less than 2% more.","zh":"将航班对气候的影响减少半数之多，所付出的代价非常小。需要降低飞行高度的航班可能并不多，仅占航班总量的5%。由于飞行高度越高，燃油效率越高，这些降低飞行高度的航班会消耗更多航空燃油，但增加量不到2%。"},{"index":6,"en":"Burning even that little extra fuel would be anathema to airlines. So some suggest the costs of action might be minimised, and the airlines incentivised, by setting up a market which somehow links contrail cooling to carbon prices. The European Union, which has had some success and plenty of experience with carbon markets, recently took a small step towards something along these lines. It is also the sort of idea to which economists—and The Economist—tend to be partial. But it would be a mistake nonetheless.","zh":"哪怕只是多烧这么一点点燃油，也是航空公司极其反感的。因此，有人提出，可以建立一种将尾迹云带来的降温效应与碳价格联系起来的市场机制，以尽可能降低采取相关措施的成本，同时为航空公司提供激励。欧盟在碳市场方面不仅取得了一定成效，也积累了丰富经验，最近已朝着这一方向迈出了一小步。这也是经济学家，包括《经济学人》在内，往往比较偏爱的思路之一。但即便如此，这样做仍然是错误的。"},{"index":7,"en":"Markets for pollutants have worked best when both the aim and the remedy are fairly simple—most famously, reducing sulphur-dioxide emissions from power stations in America. Contrails, by contrast, are complicated. Though there is no doubt that their net effect is warming, saying how much warming a particular contrail might produce is often difficult and sometimes next to impossible.","zh":"在目标明确，而且解决办法相对简单时，污染物交易市场运转得最为成功。最著名的例子是，美国减少发电厂二氧化硫排放的做法。相比之下，尾迹云要复杂得多。尽管毫无疑问，尾迹云总体上会产生增温效应，但要判断某一片特定的尾迹云究竟可能造成多大程度的增温，往往非常困难，有时甚至几乎不可能。"},{"index":8,"en":"The difficulties are made yet worse when the contrail being assessed is a purely notional one—as would be the case for the contrails avoided by changing flight paths. Valuing counterfactuals is always hard.","zh":"如果被评估的尾迹云只存在于假设当中，比如可以通过改变飞行航线避免的尾迹云，问题就会更加棘手。对反事实情形进行估值，向来很困难。"},{"index":9,"en":"If contrail-avoidance turns out to be as useful as it looks, it would be much simpler to simply have air-traffic controllers assign routes that limit persistent contrails when it is possible and safe to do so. If some airlines choose to avoid the affected routes, others will surely be happy to take their place. And if such a scheme were also to show the benefits of innovations in air-traffic control (quite a few have been suggested) the industry would end up better off, as well as less polluting.","zh":"如果规避尾迹云的做法确实像目前看起来那样有效，那么最简单的办法就是：只要条件允许且安全可行，就由空中交通管制员安排能够减少持久性尾迹云的航线。如果部分航空公司选择避开受影响的航线，其他航空公司肯定会乐于填补空缺。而且，如果这种方案还能展示空中交通管制创新所带来的好处（目前已经有人提出了不少相关方案），那么最终整个航空业不仅会减少污染，也会从中获益。"}],"vocab":[{"term":"contrail","head":"n. /ˈkɒntreɪl/ (also vapor trail) a white line left in","definition":"the sky by an aircraft that consists of water vapour (= gas) that has condensed (= turned back into very small drops of","gloss":"water)飞机尾迹","example":"The fighter jets left long contrails that slowly dispersed","exampleZh":"acrossthebluesky.战斗机留下了长长的尾迹，在蓝天中缓慢 消散。","tags":[]},{"term":"thick/thin on the ground idiom if people or things are","head":"","definition":"thick/thin on the ground, there are a lot/not many of them","gloss":"inaplace为数众多（或不多）；数目巨大（或微小）；众多（或","example":"During the festival, tourists are thick on the ground in the","exampleZh":"稀少） Customers are thin on the ground at this time of year. 一年 里这个季节顾客很少。 oldtown.节日期间，老城区游客密集。","tags":[]},{"term":"undertake","head":"v. /ˌʌndəˈteɪk/ to make yourself responsible for","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"sthandstartdoingit承担；从事；负责","exampleZh":"University professors both teach and undertake research. 大 学教授既要教学又要从事研究工作。 v. to agree or promise that you will do sth 承诺；允诺；答应 He undertook to finish the job by Friday. 他答应星期五或之 前完成这一工作。","tags":[]},{"term":"streak","head":"n. /striːk/ a long thin mark or line that is a different","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"colourfromthesurfaceitison条纹；长条痕（尤指颜色不同","exampleZh":"的） There are these dark streaks on the surface of the moon. 月 亮表面有这些黑色的条纹。 在广袤的大地上，关于全球变暖的好消息寥寥无几。但在 高空之上或许还有一些转机。8月18日，英国空中交通管制服 务机构NATS与多个气候研究机构共同开展的科学研究宣布启 动，名为“蓝天行动”。研究人员专门研究飞机产生的条状云， 即所谓的飞机尾迹云对气候的影响。","tags":[]},{"term":"consortium","head":"n. /kənˈsɔːtiəm/ (pl. consortiums or consortia)","definition":"a group of people, countries, companies, etc. who are","gloss":"working together on a particular project（合作进行某项工程","example":"The consortium includes some of the biggest building","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"swathe","head":"n. /sweɪð/ (also swath /swɒθ/) a long strip or large","definition":"","gloss":"areaespeciallyofland长条区域，大块区域;（尤指）长条田地，","example":"Huge swathes of rainforest are being cleared for farming","exampleZh":"大块田地 andmining.为了耕种和采矿，大片大片的雨林被砍伐。","tags":[]},{"term":"impact","head":"n. /ˈɪmpækt/ (~ of sth) (on sb/sth) the powerful","definition":"","gloss":"effect that sth has on sb/sth 巨大影响；强大作用","example":"The report assesses the impact of AIDS on the gay The company’s performance was impacted by the high","exampleZh":"community.这个报告评估了艾滋病对同性恋群体的影响。 v. /ɪmˈpækt/ (~ on/upon sth) to have an effect on sth（对 某事物）有影响，有作用（注意重音） valueofthepound.公司的业绩受到了英镑高值的冲击。","tags":[]},{"term":"aviation","head":"n. /ˌeɪviˈeɪʃn/ the designing, building and flying of","definition":"","gloss":"aircraft 航空","example":"He has worked in commercial aviation for over twenty years.","exampleZh":"他在商业航空领域工作了二十多年。 在接下来的两个冬天，研究团队计划考察，能否通过减少 北大西洋大片空域中持久性尾迹云量，从而显著降低民航对气 候的影响。这类尾迹云产生的气候影响最大。如果这项实验取 得成功，再将这项技术应用到全球范围，或许可以将航空旅行 对气候造成的影响降低半数之多。","tags":[]},{"term":"wispy","head":"adj. /ˈwɪspi/ consisting of small, thin pieces; not thick","definition":"","gloss":"一绺绺的；一缕缕的；成束的；纤细的","example":"A few wispy clouds floated above the valley as the sun","exampleZh":"begantoset.夕阳西下时，几缕轻柔的云絮飘浮在山谷上方。","tags":[]},{"term":"cirrus cloud","head":"n. /ˈsɪrəs klaʊd/ a wispy white cloud (usually of","definition":"","gloss":"fine ice crystals) at a high altitude (4 to 8 miles) 卷云","example":"The sun was blazing from a blue sky feathered lightly with","exampleZh":"cirruscloud.阳光灿烂，蔚蓝天空中飘着些许卷云。","tags":[]},{"term":"parasol","head":"n. /ˈpærəsɒl/ a type of light umbrella that women","definition":"","gloss":"in the past carried to protect themselves from the sun（旧","example":"Due to having weak health, she is always seen with a","exampleZh":"时的）女用阳伞 parasolwhenoutside.由于身体虚弱，她外出时总是撑着阳伞。","tags":[]},{"term":"trap","head":"v. /træp/ to prevent something from escaping,","definition":"","gloss":"especially by capturing or enclosing it 困住；使无法逃脱","example":"n. an unpleasant situation from which it is hard to escape","exampleZh":"The greenhouse gases trap heat in the atmosphere. 温室气 体将热量困在大气中。 （难以逃脱的）困境，牢笼 Some women see marriage as a trap. 有些妇女把婚姻视作围 城。","tags":[]},{"term":"infrared","head":"adj. /ˌɪnfrəˈred/ having or using electromagnetic","definition":"waves which are longer than those of red light in the","gloss":"","example":"spectrum, and which cannot be seen 红外线的；使用红外线","exampleZh":"的 The bathroom could be warmed by an infrared lamp. 可以 使用红外线灯来温暖那间浴室。","tags":[]},{"term":"radiation","head":"n. /ˌreɪdiˈeɪʃn/ powerful and very dangerous rays","definition":"","gloss":"that are sent out from radioactive substances 辐射；放射线","example":"They suffer from health problems and fear the long term","exampleZh":"effectsofradiation.他们受健康问题的困扰，还担心遭受辐射 造成的长期影响。","tags":[]},{"term":"handsomely","head":"adv. /ˈhænsəmli/ very well or to a great","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"degree可观地","exampleZh":"Their strategy paid off handsomely. 他们的策略得到了可观的 回报。","tags":[]},{"term":"outweigh","head":"v. /ˌaʊtˈweɪ/ to be greater or more important","definition":"","gloss":"thansth重于；大于；超过","example":"SYN exceed, surpass, prevail over ANT fall short of","exampleZh":"The advantages far outweigh the disadvantages. 利远大于 弊。 在阳光明媚的日子里，一些飞机尾迹云会逐渐转化为纤细 的卷云，看起来仿佛一把精巧的遮阳伞，似乎能够为地球降温。 事实上，部分尾迹云确实会让其下方的气温略有下降。但与此 同时，它们也会通过截留一部分原本会逸散到太空中的上升红 外辐射，使地球升温。平均而言，这种增温效应存在于所有尾 迹云（以及它们最终转化成的卷云）中，其作用远远超过了部 分尾迹云所带来的降温效果。从气候大局来看，尾迹云是一项 负担。","tags":[]},{"term":"supersaturated","head":"adj. /ˌsjuːpəˈsætʃəreɪtɪd/ containing more","definition":"","gloss":"of a substance than can be absorbed 超饱和的","example":"Meteorologists are studying how supersaturated air masses","exampleZh":"trigger the formation of ice crystals. 气象学家正在研究过饱 和气团如何触发冰晶的形成。","tags":[]},{"term":"altitude","head":"n. /ˈæltɪtjuːd/ the height above sea level 海拔；海","definition":"","gloss":"拔高度；高程","example":"(Words of Similar Form) attitude n. /ˈætɪtjuːd/ (~ to/towards sb/sth) the way that you think and feel about sb/sth; the way that you behave towards sb/sth that shows","exampleZh":"We are flying at an altitude of 6 000 metres. 我们的飞行高度 是6000米。 how you think and feel 态度；看法 Being unemployed produces negative attitudes to work. 失 业会对工作产生消极态度。","tags":[]},{"term":"integrate","head":"v. /ˈɪntɪɡreɪt/ (~ A) (into/with B) （~ A and B） to","definition":"combine two or more things so that they work together; to","gloss":"combine with sth else in this way（使）合并，成为一体","example":"These programs will integrate with your existing software.","exampleZh":"这些程序将和你的已有软件可综合成整体。 好在，似乎只需对飞行航线做些小幅调整，就能避免其中 相当一部分危害。持久性尾迹云只会出现在所谓的“冰过饱和 区”内。飞机往往只需稍微降低飞行高度，就可以避开这些区 域。“蓝天行动”的目的，就是弄清楚以下几个问题：ISSR的 存在能否被准确预测；如此小幅的高度调整在多大程度上能够 有效避免持久性尾迹云；以及，为实现这一目的所需的航线调 整，如何能以便捷且安全的方式纳入航空公司和空中交通管制 的日常运行流程。","tags":[]},{"term":"cut","head":"n. /kʌt/ (~ in sth) a reduction in amount, size, supply,","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"etc.（数量、尺寸、供应等的）削减，减少，缩减","exampleZh":"They had to take a 20% cut in pay. 他们不得不接受减薪 20%。 n. a share in sth, especially money（尤指钱的）份，份额 They were rewarded with a cut of 5% from the profits. 他们 得到了占利润5%份额的酬报。 a cut above sb/sth idiombetter than sb/sth 优于；比…高一 等；胜……一筹 His latest novel is a cut above the rest. 他最近出版的小说比 其他的小说都好。","tags":[]},{"term":"buy","head":"v. /baɪ/ if you buy something like time, freedom, or","definition":"victory, you obtain it but only by offering or giving up","gloss":"something in return 换取","example":"v. to persuade sb to do sth dishonest in return for money","exampleZh":"It was a risky operation, but might buy more time. 这是一项 冒险的举动，但也许能换得更多的时间。 买通；收买；贿赂 Hecan’tbebought.他是收买不了的。 v. to obtain sth by losing sth else of great value 付出极大的 代价而获得 Her fame was bought at the expense of her marriage. 她出 了名，却牺牲了她的婚姻。 将航班对气候的影响减少半数之多，所付出的代价非常小。 需要降低飞行高度的航班可能并不多，仅占航班总量的5%。由 于飞行高度越高，燃油效率越高，这些降低飞行高度的航班会 消耗更多航空燃油，但增加量不到2%。","tags":[]},{"term":"anathema","head":"n. /əˈnæθəmə/ (formal) a thing or an idea which","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"you hate because it is the opposite of what you believe 可","exampleZh":"憎的事物；可恶的想法 For older employees, the new system is an anathema. 对于 年纪较大的职员来说，新制度就是眼中钉，肉中刺。","tags":[]},{"term":"incentivise","head":"v. /ɪnˈsentɪvaɪz/ (also incentivize) to make","definition":"","gloss":"someone want to do something 刺激，激励","example":"We need to incentivize our sales managers to achieve these","exampleZh":"targets.我们需要激励我们的销售经理实现这些目标。","tags":[]},{"term":"partial","head":"adj. /ˈpɑːʃl/ having a liking for something 偏爱…的，","definition":"","gloss":"喜欢…的","example":"The general has ordered a partial withdrawal of troops from","exampleZh":"I’mnotpartialtofish.我并不特别爱吃鱼。 adj. not complete or whole 部分的；不完全的 thearea.将军已下令部队部分人员撤出该地区。 哪怕只是多烧这么一点点燃油，也是航空公司极其反感的。 因此，有人提出，可以建立一种将尾迹云带来的降温效应与碳 价格联系起来的市场机制，以尽可能降低采取相关措施的成本， 同时为航空公司提供激励。欧盟在碳市场方面不仅取得了一定 成效，也积累了丰富经验，最近已朝着这一方向迈出了一小步。 这也是经济学家，包括《经济学人》在内，往往比较偏爱的思 路之一。但即便如此，这样做仍然是错误的。","tags":[]},{"term":"sulphur","head":"n. /ˈsʌlfə(r)/ (NAmE sulfur) (symbol S) a chemical","definition":"element. Sulphur is a pale yellow substance that produces a strong unpleasant smell when it burns and is used in","gloss":"medicine and industry. 硫；硫磺","example":"The laboratory assistant detected a faint smell of burning","exampleZh":"sulphuraftertheexperiment.实验助理在实验后闻到了轻微的 硫磺燃烧气味。","tags":[]},{"term":"dioxide","head":"n. /daɪˈɒksaɪd/ a substance formed by combining","definition":"two atoms of oxygen and one atom of another chemical","gloss":"element二氧化物","example":"Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the atmosphere during","exampleZh":"photosynthesis.植物在光合作用过程中从大气中吸收二氧化碳。","tags":[]},{"term":"emission","head":"n. /iˈmɪʃn/ (formal) the production or sending out","definition":"","gloss":"oflight,heat,gas,etc.（光、热、气等的）发出，射出，排放","example":"The emission of gases such as carbon dioxide should be","exampleZh":"stabilizedattheirpresentlevel.二氧化碳之类气体的排放应该 被控制在目前的水平上。","tags":[]},{"term":"complicated","head":"adj. /ˈkɒmplɪkeɪtɪd/ made of many different","definition":"things or parts that are connected; difficult to understand","gloss":"复杂的；难懂的","example":"SYN complex, intricate","exampleZh":"The situation in Lebanon is very complicated. 黎巴嫩的形势 非常复杂。 在目标明确，而且解决办法相对简单时，污染物交易市场 运转得最为成功。最著名的例子是，美国减少发电厂二氧化硫 排放的做法。相比之下，尾迹云要复杂得多。尽管毫无疑问， 尾迹云总体上会产生增温效应，但要判断某一片特定的尾迹云 究竟可能造成多大程度的增温，往往非常困难，有时甚至几乎 不可能。","tags":[]},{"term":"yet","head":"adv. /jet/ (~ worse, more importantly, etc.) used to","definition":"emphasize an increase in the degree of sth (= how bad,","gloss":"important,etc.itis)（强调程度的增加）更","example":"The new software is fast, but the upgraded version is yet adv. (could, might, may, etc. do sth ~) used to say that sth could, might, etc. happen in the future, even though it adv. from now until the period of time mentioned has","exampleZh":"faster.新软件很快，但升级版甚至更快。 seemsunlikely（表示将来可能发生，尽管现在似乎没有可能） 早晚，总有一天 Shecouldyetsurpriseusall.总有一天，她会让我们都大吃一 惊。 adv. now; as soon as this 现在；即刻；马上 We don’t need to start yet. 我们不必马上开始。 passed从现在起直至某一时间；还 They won’t arrive for at least two hours yet. 他们至少要过 两个小时才能到。","tags":[]},{"term":"assess","head":"v. /əˈses/ (~ sb/sth as sth) to make a judgement","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"about the nature or quality of sb/sth 评估，评定（性质、质","exampleZh":"量） It’s difficult to assess the effects of these changes. 这些变 化带来的效果难以评估。 前缀：as-朝，向，加强 assistv./əˈsɪst/帮助（as-朝，向，加强+sist站立） assurev./əˈʃʊə(r)/保证（as-朝，向，加强+sure肯定）","tags":[]},{"term":"assimilate","head":"v. /əˈsɪməleɪt/ (使)同化（as- 朝，向，加强 +","definition":"","gloss":"","example":"simil-类似，一样+-ate做，造成）","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"counterfactual","head":"n. /ˌkaʊntəˈfæktʃuəl/ expressing what has","definition":"not happened but could, would, or might under differing","gloss":"conditions 反事实的","example":"Thoughts about how an embarrassing event might have turned out differently are known to psychologists as","exampleZh":"counterfactualthinking.心理学家把人们想象已发生的尴尬事 件其实可能以不同方式发生这样的想法叫做违实思考。 如果被评估的尾迹云只存在于假设当中，比如可以通过改 变飞行航线避免的尾迹云，问题就会更加棘手。对反事实情形 进行估值，向来很困难。","tags":[]},{"term":"assign","head":"v. /əˈsaɪn/ (~ sth to sb) (~ sb sth) to give sb sth that","definition":"","gloss":"they can use, or some work or responsibility 分配（某物）；","example":"The teacher assigned a different task to each of the children. v. (~ sb to sth/as sth) to provide a person for a particular","exampleZh":"分派，布置（工作、任务等） The two large classrooms have been assigned to us. 这两间 大教室分配给了我们。 老师给每个儿童布置的作业都不相同。 task or position 指定；指派 They’ve assigned their best man to the job. 他们指派了最 优秀的人担任这项工作。","tags":[]},{"term":"scheme","head":"n. /skiːm/ a plan or system for doing or organizing","definition":"","gloss":"sth计划；方案；体系；体制","example":"Under the new scheme only successful schools will be given","exampleZh":"extrafunding.在新体制下，只有办得好的学校才可获得额外经 费。","tags":[]},{"term":"welloffadj.rich富有的，有钱的","head":"","definition":"","gloss":"a well-off neighbourhood 富人区","example":"(Para. 2) Over the next two winters the consortium aims to see if it is possible to reduce the number of persistent contrails—the class with the largest such effects—over a swathe of the North Atlantic, thereby Para. 2 Over the next two winters the consortium aims to see if it is possible to reduce the number of persistent contrails— the class with the largest such effects—over a swathe of the North Atlantic, thereby measurably reducing the climate Over the next two winters the consortium aims to see if it is possible to reduce the number of persistent contrails —the class with the largest such effects— over a swathe of the North Atlantic, thereby measurably reducing the climate impact of civil aviation.  up for grabs idiom something is available for anyone to  on the fence idiom unable to decide between two options out how well the presence of ISSRs can be predicted, how effective such little shifts in altitude can be in avoiding persistent contrails, and how easily and safely the changes in flight path needed to bring them about can be integrated into routines for airlines and air-traffic control. new policy brought about significant changes in the economy.  give rise to idiomto cause something to happen or to be","exampleZh":"adj. having a lot of or a number of 拥有大量…的；充足的 The city is well off for parks and gardens. 这座城市有很多公 园和花园。 如果规避尾迹云的做法确实像目前看起来那样有效，那么 最简单的办法就是：只要条件允许且安全可行，就由空中交通 管制员安排能够减少持久性尾迹云的航线。如果部分航空公司 选择避开受影响的航线，其他航空公司肯定会乐于填补空缺。 而且，如果这种方案还能展示空中交通管制创新所带来的好处 （目前已经有人提出了不少相关方案），那么最终整个航空业 不仅会减少污染，也会从中获益。 August 15TH- 21ST ｜Leaders 公告学习流程精读， 供句子分析） 今日句子分析 impactofcivilaviation.在接下来的两个冬天，研究团队计划考察， 能否通过减少北大西洋大片空域中持久性尾迹云量，从而显著降低 民航对气候的影响。这类尾迹云产生的气候影响最大。 主句 时间状语 主语谓语 宾语从句 形式主语系语表语真正的主语 宾语 同位语后置定语 地点状语 结果状语 后置定语 主句： 时间状语：Over the next two winters； 主语：the consortium；谓语：aims to see； 宾语从句： 引导词：if；形式主语：it；系语：is；表语：possible；真正的主 语：to reduce； 宾语：the number of persistent contrails； 同位语：the class；后置定语：with the largest such effects；(进 一步说明persistentcontrails是什么性质的尾迹云，可理解为“持 久性尾迹云，即其中气候影响最大的一类”。这里的class表示“类 别、类型”，such是回指，指代前文刚刚提到的性质。 译文重新调整为“这类尾迹云产生的气候影响最大”，汉语使用主 谓结构更加自然。由于这部分内容仅为补充说明，较为次要，因此 放在句子最后，优先保证主干的连贯性。) 地点状语：over a swathe of the North Atlantic；（over 表示在 “在……上空/覆盖……范围”，没有搭配动词，进一步说明这些尾 迹云出现在哪里。） 结果状语：thereby measurably reducing the climate impact； （thereby表示“由此，从而，因此”，语言风格很正式，常见于 学术论文、法律文本、正式报告等，口语中很少用到。后加V-ing， 这就是reducing的由来。注意区分它和therefore，therefore强 调的是逻辑结论：The weather was bad. Therefore, the flight wascancelled.（天气不好，因此航班取消了。）thereby强调的是 通过某种动作/手段，从而产生某个结果：Theairlinechangedthe flight path, thereby reducing emissions. （航空公司调整了航线， 从而减少了排放。）本文就是这个逻辑，所以译文增译了“通过”， 把原文隐含的“手段—结果”关系显化。） 后置定语：of civil aviation； 写作积累 1. （Para. 1）But there may be some up in the air. 本句中的 up in the air 表示“high in the clouds”的同时，也 表示 “uncertain, often because other matters have to be decidedfirst”，即“尚未有定论，悬而未决，尚未决定”，例如， Our travel plans are still up in the air. 我们的旅行计划尚未决定。 这里是原作者设置的双关。此外，还有以下习语可以表示相类似的 含义： take,win,orclaim待价而沽，谁都能拿，尚未定论 The ad says, “ World’s Greatest Job, Up for Grabs. ” 广 告上说：“世界上最棒的工作，虚位以待。” or refuse to take a side in an argument 犹豫不决，左右为难 The committee is still on the fence about the proposal. 委 员会对这项提案仍然犹豫不决。 2. （Para. 4）The purpose of Operation Blue Skies is to find 本句中的 bring about 表示“to cause something to happen ormakeachangeoccur”，即“带来，引起，实现”，例如，The 新政策引起了经济上的重大变化。此外，还有以下习语可以表示相 同的含义，供写作时选用： the origin of a result 引起 The new policy will give rise to much discussion. 这项新 政策将引起很多讨论。  set off idiomcause something to start 触发，引发 The announcement set off a wave of protests. 这项声明引发 了一波抗议。","tags":[]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】8.30 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 1 and 2, Operation Blue Skies aims to _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"require airlines worldwide to change flight paths as soon as the study begins"},{"key":"B","text":"prove that contrails are merely a visual nuisance rather than a climate problem"},{"key":"C","text":"test whether persistent contrails over the North Atlantic can be measurably reduced"},{"key":"D","text":"design aircraft engines that can eliminate both contrails and carbon-dioxide emissions"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·研究目的识别","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 1-2","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：Operation Blue Skies...is a scientific study being undertaken by Britain's air-traffic-control service, NATS, and various organisations where people study the effects on climate of...contrails.","- 原文（Para.2）：Over the next two winters the consortium aims to see if it is possible to reduce the number of persistent contrails...over a swathe of the North Atlantic, thereby measurably reducing the climate impact of civil aviation.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：过度推理陷阱。全球应用只是实验成功后 may 产生的可能性，实验本身并不立即强制全球航空公司改变航路。","- 选项B（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。研究的出发点正是 contrails 会影响气候，而不是证明它们只是视觉问题。","- 选项C（正确）：Para.2 明确说 consortium aims to see if it is possible to reduce persistent contrails over a swathe of the North Atlantic，并使民用航空的气候影响可测量地降低。C 项准确概括研究目的。","- 选项D（错误）：无中生有陷阱。研究关注航路和尾迹 avoidance，没有提出设计消除尾迹和二氧化碳排放的新发动机。","【命题技巧】","- 研究目的定位：aims to see if 是目的题的显性信号。","- 范围限定：North Atlantic 是实验范围，worldwide 是成功后可能推广的范围。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 3 that contrails are a climate liability because _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"their heat-trapping effect is on average larger than the limited cooling some of them provide"},{"key":"B","text":"all contrails cool the air beneath them by reflecting incoming sunlight"},{"key":"C","text":"cirrus clouds prevent every kind of infrared radiation from reaching the earth"},{"key":"D","text":"their warming effect is usually slightly smaller than their cooling effect"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】推理判断题·净效应推理","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3","【解析】","- 原文（Para.3）：And some contrails do indeed cool things down beneath them a bit.","- 原文（Para.3）：But they also warm things up by trapping some of the upwelling infrared radiation that would otherwise escape into space.","- 原文（Para.3）：On average, that warming effect, found in all contrails (and the cirrus clouds they turn into), handsomely outweighs the cooling provided by some.","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：作者先承认部分尾迹有轻微冷却作用，再用 But 转折指出所有尾迹都会通过拦截向上红外辐射而增温，且平均而言增温显著超过冷却。A 项概括了净效应为负的原因。","- 选项B（错误）：过度推理陷阱。原文只说 some contrails 冷却下方空气，不是所有尾迹都通过反射阳光降温。","- 选项C（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。卷云拦截的是本应逃逸到太空的向上红外辐射，不是阻止所有红外辐射到达地面。","- 选项D（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。原文说 warming effect handsomely outweighs cooling，增温大于冷却，不是略小于冷却。","【命题技巧】","- 转折后重心：But 与 On average 提示净效应方向。","- 限定词对比：some cooling 与 warming found in all contrails 是解题关键。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"Which of the following is true about the proposed changes to flight paths in Paragraphs 4 and 5?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Persistent contrails are likely to appear wherever commercial aircraft choose to cruise."},{"key":"B","text":"About 5% of flights might fly lower, and those flights would burn less than 2% more fuel."},{"key":"C","text":"Small altitude changes are expected to remove almost all of aviation's climate effects at no cost."},{"key":"D","text":"Airlines and air-traffic controllers have already integrated the new routines into daily operation."}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·正误判断","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 4-5","【解析】","- 原文（Para.4）：Persistent contrails appear only in what are known as \"ice-supersaturated regions\" (ISSRs). Often planes can avoid such regions just by flying a little bit lower.","- 原文（Para.4）：The purpose of Operation Blue Skies is to find out how well the presence of ISSRs can be predicted...and how easily and safely the changes in flight path...can be integrated into routines for airlines and air-traffic control.","- 原文（Para.5）：The number of flights at lowered altitude might be small—as little as 5% of the total...those flights would consume more jet fuel, but less than 2% more.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。持续尾迹只出现在冰过饱和区，不是任何商业飞机巡航处都会形成。","- 选项B（正确）：原文给出两个数字：降低高度的航班可能只占总数 5%，且这些航班燃油增加不到 2%。B 项同时保留比例与限定。","- 选项C（错误）：过度推理陷阱。全球推广最多可能把航空旅行气候影响减少一半，且仍有小幅燃油成本，不是零成本消除几乎所有影响。","- 选项D（错误）：时态错位陷阱。实验要检验这些航路变化能否安全整合进日常运行，说明尚未完全整合。","【命题技巧】","- 数字归属：5% 指 lowered-altitude flights，2% 指这些航班的额外燃油，不能换主语。","- 实验与现状区分：aims to find out 与 already integrated 形成时间对立。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"The author argues in Paragraphs 6 to 8 that a market linking contrail avoidance to carbon prices would be mistaken mainly because _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the European Union has already proved that such a market can value avoided contrails accurately"},{"key":"B","text":"economists generally refuse to accept pollution markets unless they deal with carbon-dioxide emissions"},{"key":"C","text":"airlines should be allowed to ignore climate costs whenever extra fuel consumption is very small"},{"key":"D","text":"the warming effect of a particular or counterfactual contrail is often too difficult to measure"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】作者态度题·论证理由识别","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 6-8","【解析】","- 原文（Para.6）：So some suggest...setting up a market which somehow links contrail cooling to carbon prices...But it would be a mistake nonetheless.","- 原文（Para.7）：Markets for pollutants have worked best when both the aim and the remedy are fairly simple...Contrails, by contrast, are complicated...saying how much warming a particular contrail might produce is often difficult and sometimes next to impossible.","- 原文（Para.8）：The difficulties are made yet worse when the contrail being assessed is a purely notional one—as would be the case for the contrails avoided by changing flight paths. Valuing counterfactuals is always hard.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。欧盟只是朝相关方向迈出一小步，作者随后指出该市场仍是错误；原文没有说欧盟已证明能准确估值。","- 选项B（错误）：无中生有陷阱。原文反而说经济学家和《经济学人》通常倾向这类市场，作者是在此背景下提出保留意见。","- 选项C（错误）：答非所问陷阱。额外燃油少是成本低的证据，不是作者允许航空公司忽视气候成本；作者主张通过空管分配航路来减少尾迹。","- 选项D（正确）：作者的反对理由集中在可测量性：特定尾迹的增温效应难以量化，而被避免的尾迹更是反事实对象，估值难度更大。D 项抓住 market 机制失灵的核心。","【命题技巧】","- 让步转折结构：作者承认污染市场有成功经验和经济学吸引力，再用 But 提出关键限定。","- 抽象概念落地：notional contrail 与 counterfactual 是困难题的核心概念。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"What is the main idea of the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Aviation should be grounded until contrails can be removed from all flight paths."},{"key":"B","text":"Operation Blue Skies aims to replace existing carbon markets with a new airline subsidy system."},{"key":"C","text":"Small flight-path changes could reduce aviation's climate impact and should be managed through air-traffic control."},{"key":"D","text":"Contrails are so complex that airlines and governments should take no action until measurement is perfect."}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·全文概括","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（副标题）：Fewer contrails would be good for the climate.","- 原文（Para.2）：...a worldwide application of the same techniques might cut the climate effects of air travel by as much as half.","- 原文（Para.9）：If contrail-avoidance turns out to be as useful as it looks, it would be much simpler to simply have air-traffic controllers assign routes that limit persistent contrails when it is possible and safe to do so.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：过度推理陷阱。原文建议调整航路而非停飞航空业；尾迹只在特定区域且可安全绕开。","- 选项B（错误）：偷换概念陷阱。Operation Blue Skies 是科学实验，不是取代碳市场的补贴制度；作者反对的是把尾迹纳入市场机制。","- 选项C（正确）：全文逻辑是：尾迹净增温，小幅降低高度可避免持续尾迹，成本较小；作者最后主张由空管在安全可行时分配航路，而不是建立难测量的尾迹市场。C 项完整概括方案与机制。","- 选项D（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。测量复杂只是反对交易市场的理由，不是不采取行动；作者明确提出 simpler 的空管方案。","【命题技巧】","- 方案型主旨：科学报道后接评论时，主旨须同时包含问题、方案与作者偏好的实施机制。","- 极端选项排除：grounded、no action 等极端表达与原文渐进改革立场不符。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】8.30检验题__完型填空(1).docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["Over the next two winters the consortium aims to see if it is possible to reduce the number of persistent contrails—the class with the largest such effects—over a swathe of the North Atlantic, thereby measurably reducing the climate ____【11】____ of civil aviation. If this experiment works, a worldwide ____【12】____ of the same techniques might cut the climate effects of air travel by as much as half.","And some contrails do indeed cool things down beneath them a bit. But they also warm things up by ____【13】____ some of the upwelling infrared radiation that would otherwise ____【14】____ into space. On average, that warming effect, found in all contrails, handsomely ____【15】____ the cooling provided by some. In the climate scheme of things, contrails are a ____【16】____.","Happily, it appears that much harm can be ____【17】____ by small changes to flight paths. Persistent contrails appear only in what are known as “ice-supersaturated regions”. Often planes can avoid such regions just by flying a little bit ____【18】____.","The reduction of up to half in the climate-effects of air travel would come at a very small ____【19】____. The number of flights at lowered altitude might be ____【20】____—as little as 5% of the total."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"impact"},{"key":"B","text":"history"},{"key":"C","text":"cost"},{"key":"D","text":"speed"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (impact)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·气候语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第1句","【解析】","[A] impact（影响）：climate impact of civil aviation 指民航的气候影响。正确答案。","[B] history（历史）：语义无关。语义场干扰。","[C] cost（成本）：成本话题在后文，本句强调气候效应。语义场干扰。","[D] speed（速度）：与气候研究目标无关。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"abandonment"},{"key":"B","text":"application"},{"key":"C","text":"design"},{"key":"D","text":"description"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (application)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·方案推广","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] abandonment（放弃）：与 works 后推广技术的逻辑相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] application（应用）：worldwide application of the same techniques 指全球应用同一方法。正确答案。","[C] design（设计）：技术已经试验，不是重新设计。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] description（描述）：描述不能直接减少影响。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"releasing"},{"key":"B","text":"trapping"},{"key":"C","text":"reflecting"},{"key":"D","text":"amplifying"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (trapping)","analysis":["【题型】非谓语动词·物理机制","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] releasing（释放）：方向相反，暖效应来自留住辐射。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] trapping（截留）：trapping infrared radiation 指截留向上的红外辐射。正确答案。","[C] reflecting（反射）：反射辐射可能带来冷却，与 warm things up 矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] amplifying（放大）：语义过泛，不能说明辐射被留住的机制。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"return"},{"key":"B","text":"converge"},{"key":"C","text":"disappear"},{"key":"D","text":"escape"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (escape)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·方向搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] return（返回）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] converge（汇聚）：与 into space 的方向不符。搭配干扰。","[C] disappear（消失）：语义可通，但不如 escape into space 精准。近义干扰。","[D] escape（逃逸）：would otherwise escape into space 是气候物理常见表达。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"matches"},{"key":"B","text":"offsets"},{"key":"C","text":"outweighs"},{"key":"D","text":"cancels"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (outweighs)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·数量比较","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第3句","【解析】","[A] matches（相当）：与 handsomely 和净变暖结论不符。程度差异干扰。","[B] offsets（抵消）：方向相反，变暖效应不是抵消而是超过冷却效应。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] outweighs（超过）：warming effect outweighs the cooling effect 指暖效应大于冷效应。正确答案。","[D] cancels（抵消）：语义过强且方向不符。程度差异干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"benefit"},{"key":"B","text":"liability"},{"key":"C","text":"mystery"},{"key":"D","text":"signal"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (liability)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·态度总结","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第4句","【解析】","[A] benefit（益处）：与 net warming 和 liability 相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] liability（负担、不利因素）：气候语境中 liability 指负面资产。正确答案。","[C] mystery（谜）：研究已有明确净效应判断。语义场干扰。","[D] signal（信号）：语义无关。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"caused"},{"key":"B","text":"measured"},{"key":"C","text":"ignored"},{"key":"D","text":"avoided"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (avoided)","analysis":["【题型】非谓语动词·被动语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] caused（造成）：与 harm can be avoided 语义相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] measured（测量）：测量危害不等于减少危害。语义场干扰。","[C] ignored（忽视）：忽视危害不是解决办法。语义场干扰。","[D] avoided（避免）：harm can be avoided by small changes 指通过小调整避免危害。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lower"},{"key":"B","text":"higher"},{"key":"C","text":"faster"},{"key":"D","text":"longer"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (lower)","analysis":["【题型】形容词/副词辨析·方位语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第3句","【解析】","[A] lower（更低）：flying a little bit lower 与后文 lowered altitude 呼应。正确答案。","[B] higher（更高）：方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] faster（更快）：速度不是避开过饱和区的调整。语义场干扰。","[D] longer（更久）：时间语义不符。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"price"},{"key":"B","text":"budget"},{"key":"C","text":"cost"},{"key":"D","text":"penalty"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (cost)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·搭配语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 4, 第1句","【解析】","[A] price（价格）：可指油价或票价，不是 come at a small ___ 的自然宾语。搭配干扰。","[B] budget（预算）：预算规模语义过具体，本句指付出的代价。语义场干扰。","[C] cost（成本、代价）：come at a very small cost 指以很小的代价实现。正确答案。","[D] penalty（处罚）：语义过重且不符。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"large"},{"key":"B","text":"fixed"},{"key":"C","text":"variable"},{"key":"D","text":"small"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (small)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·数据呼应","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 4, 第2句","【解析】","[A] large（大的）：与 as little as 5% 矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] fixed（固定的）：文中 as little as 表明数量很小且非固定。语义场干扰。","[C] variable（可变的）：强调点是小比例，不是变化性。语义场干扰。","[D] small（小的）：small 与 as little as 5% of the total 呼应。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"8.30 精读(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":762219,"date":"2026-08-30","range":"","title":"Without a trace","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.30 精读(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.30 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":57581,"date":"2026-08-30","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.30 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.30检验题__完型填空(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":58683,"date":"2026-08-30","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.30检验题__完型填空(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"layout","label":"杂志排版","file":"8.30杂志排版(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":813802,"date":"2026-08-30","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.30杂志排版(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
